{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q137801734","formula":"C₁₇H₂₄N₂O₂","hill":"C17H24N2O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":17.0,"H":24.0,"N":2.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"4-AcO-EPT"},"descriptions":{"en":"4-AcO-EPT, also known as 4-acetoxy-N-ethyl-N-propyltryptamine, is a psychedelic drug of the tryptamine and 4-hydroxytryptamine families related to 4-AcO-DMT (psilacetin). It is the acetate ester of 4-HO-EPT (eprocin) and is thought to act as a prodrug of 4-HO-EPT. Based on online anecdotal reports, 4-AcO-EPT is said to have a dose of 20 to 30 mg orally. It shows reduced affinity and agonistic potency at serotonin receptors, including the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor, compared to 4-HO-EPT. Similarly to 4-HO-EPT, 4-AcO-EPT produces the head-twitch response, a behavioral proxy of psychedelic effects, in rodents, and does so with comparable potency, in line with it being a prodrug."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":138454311,"mass":288.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCN(CC)CCC1=CNC2=C1C(=CC=C2)OC(=O)C","inchikey":"VMFRFQVZMZGHOK-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"[3-[2-[ethyl(propyl)amino]ethyl]-1H-indol-4-yl] acetate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"138454311","atoms":45,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.218,"y":0.153,"z":1.594,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.83,"y":0.008,"z":2.194,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.989,"y":-1.155,"z":1.641,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.552,"y":-1.137,"z":0.237,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.554,"y":-1.544,"z":-0.755,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.184,"y":-2.91,"z":-0.494,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.887,"y":0.135,"z":-0.114,"el":"C"},{"x":0.004,"y":0.042,"z":-1.366,"el":"C"},{"x":0.876,"y":1.249,"z":-1.542,"el":"C"},{"x":0.662,"y":2.284,"z":-2.433,"el":"C"},{"x":1.689,"y":3.18,"z":-2.309,"el":"N"},{"x":2.572,"y":2.762,"z":-1.342,"el":"C"},{"x":2.094,"y":1.548,"z":-0.842,"el":"C"},{"x":2.848,"y":0